WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.830
- So I have to say. The Rock
was your last match, right?

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:06.300
So in the ring he actually
whispered something in your ear.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.483
So what did he say?

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.140
- We're Wrestlemania 19 in Seattle

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.100
and there was probably a
70 to 75,000 people there

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.660
we sold it out, Rock and I headlined

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.160
through Wrestlemania together,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.620
which no one has ever done.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.090
And he knew that after that match

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.550
I was gonna retire and
ride off into the sunset.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.250
And he knew that I didn't wanna retire,

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.740
but you know, I have some
nerve and neck issues

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.590
and I needed to get out of the business.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.110
And after the three
count, after he pinned me,

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.227
after three rock bottoms, he just said,

00:00:34.227 --> 00:00:36.897
"Man, I can't think enough
for what you did for me.

00:00:36.897 --> 00:00:38.940
"I just want you to know, I love you man."

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.773
- Aww.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.870
- And, and I'm laying there

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.730
and we got 70,000 people.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:43.870
There's a couple of
million people watching

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.850
on pay-per-view and you know,

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.920
I just kinda looked up at him, I said,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.547
I think I had my eyes closed, I said,

00:00:49.547 --> 00:00:51.140
"I love you, too."

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.480
Verbatim.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.210
And it's been a deal where, you know,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.910
Rock and I have been great friends

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.050
from when he first came into the company

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.940
and we turned it into a rivalry.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.490
And at many times, you know,
when he was the bad guy

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.500
or I was the bad guy, and
when we were both good guys,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.210
we always had a great friendship

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.070
and a lot of respect and a
lot of love for each other.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.620
And the thing about The Rock was

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.480
he was one of, probably
my most favorite opponent.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.580
He brought out the best in me

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.270
and I brought out the best in him.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.170
And when you put the two number one guys

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.740
in there together, magic happens.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.700
- Yeah I love, I love
when chemistry happens

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.110
like that, like in any kind of form

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.090
when people are working together.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.410
It's just like if it's in a TV show

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.540
or in WWE, or if it's in a movie,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.420
whatever it is, or musically
speaking, it's so cool.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.853
And that you feel it, you
feel that kind of energy.

